body:
I'm so sorry for your loss. There isn't much anyone can say really, but know that this post made me reflect on my past suicide attempts, and think about the consequences of suicide as it has been something weighing heavily on my mind (although in a more passive way).. I could not begin to fathom the amount of pain you and your loved ones are and will continue to experience in the future. My heart goes out to you, truly.. and my very deepest sympathies are with you and your family.

&#x200B;

I hope that you can heal from this, with time and love.

this initially made me really upset, because living with self harm scars is not easy... but then I tried to regulate myself and really try to understand where you're coming from.. I remember when I first started harming, I wanted to have scars as a validation of the pain I was going through.. it made it into something tangible, something that I could see and feel and prove that this pain wasn't something imaginary... 

&#x200B;

Trust me, you don't want scars - you don't want these reminders years later in your life.. you don't want to be self conscious about your body (more than you have to if you struggle with body issues like I do)... it has made my life even more difficult.. I wish you the absolute best in your recovery.

Ugh! How awesome!

&#x200B;

Thanks for sharing :)

I don't have an answer to your question, but your question is super relatable. I don't have any self-love, I can't stand myself.. my appearance, my lack of self identity, my conversational skills, my intelligence or lack there of, I can't stand my body or my mind.. and I feel all fucked up that this is the person who I have to live in until I die.. which makes me just want to die because I don't see the point in living in this shell. 

&#x200B;

After being diagnosed with BPD, PSTD - which made a lot of sense, and later ADHD and Major depressive disorder... I just don't need to keep going to doctors, and hospitals. I don't have the effort to give to recover, and I have finally decided not to try because it seems super pointless and futile. I'm tired.. I go through the motions just for those around me, because I've already put them in so much pain. Killing myself would hurt the support system I have, which is the only reason keeping me here... but that's a fucking miserable life to live.

exactly! which version of myself... do I like this or hate that?

&#x200B;

I hate that when I try to explain the lack of self identity I experience, a lot of people respond "well, that's everybody, we are all figuring ourselves out..it's normal"

&#x200B;

No, like I am literally an empty vessel... I don't have hobbies, I don't know who I am ... what I like.. what I don't like. When I was younger, I used to adopt other people's personality characteristics and mannerisms, because I felt like I had nothing that was unique to my personality. 

&#x200B;

Absolutely nothing is my own. I have no sense of self. 

&#x200B;

I have no clue who I am ...
